    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured address form so it fully satisfies the spec, with all tests passing.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to the `OwnerFields` schema (shared by request and response), documented `address` as the composed/backward-compatible field, and removed `address` from the `required` list so both the flat and structured forms \u2014 and earlier minimal owners \u2014 remain valid.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persisted `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with getters/setters so the structured lines survive the GET reload and appear in the response.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns at the end of the `owners` table (position chosen to keep the positional `INSERT`s in `data.sql` valid; hsqldb's seed inserts got two trailing `NULL`s to match).\n\n4. **`AddressNormalizer.compose(line1, line2)`** \u2014 New helper that normalizes both lines and returns `line1`, appending a single space and `line2` when the second line is present.\n\n5. **`ValidateOwner`** \u2014 Now normalizes whichever address fields are supplied, prefers the structured form when `addressLine1` is non-blank (falling back to the flat `address`), stores the composed value as `address`, and treats the owner as valid when it supplies an address in **either** form plus city.\n\n6. **`ApplyOwner`** (PUT path) \u2014 Copies the structured lines onto the entity; the create path already maps them via MapStruct.\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 structured normalization/composition (`address` == normalized `addressLine1`) and continued acceptance of the flat form \u2014 both pass, along with the full suite.",
